stallion milestone 1: board-neutral early console, RAM log, PSCI reset

One SWEET kernel for both phones. Board facts now come from the loader at
run time instead of sweet constants:

- Early framebuffer = boot_args->Video (the shim fills it; v_baseAddr 0 =
  none). start.s draws the stage-0 band and maps the 32MB block holding
  v_baseAddr only when there is one (and only into a free V=P slot);
  sweet_early.c takes width/height/stride from boot_args. sweet's shim
  passes 0x9c000000 1080x2400 as before, so sweet behaves as before.
- RAM log: ADT /sweet-ramlog reg = <phys size> is a Linux ramoops
  persistent RAM zone (sig 0x43474244, start, size, data). The early console
  appends there too: VA=PA Device block in the bootstrap tables right after
  PE_init_platform (earlier output is replayed from a 4K buffer), a kernel
  VA alias across arm_vm_init (VM_MIN_KERNEL_ADDRESS + 2 * 32MB, next to the
  framebuffer alias), then a permanent ml_io_map + serial device
  (SERIAL_SWEET_RAMLOG) so kprintf/console output keeps going there.
  It continues after the text the shim left (shim writes start = 0).
  stallion: ramoops console zone 0xfd3ff000 + 0x200000, read back from
  Android as /sys/fs/pstore/console-ramoops-0 after a warm reset.
- Reset policy from ADT /chosen (boot-args override):
  sweet-panic-reset (ms, sweetpanicreset=): panic_spin_forever and
  halt_all_cpus end in PSCI SYSTEM_RESET (smc 0x84000009) after the delay;
  sweet-reset-after (s, sweetreset=): unconditional PSCI reset that long
  after SweetPlatformExpert::start (hang watchdog, thread call).
  Neither property exists in sweet's ADT: sweet still spins on panic.

